## Quality Gate Criteria

For each research file, check:

### Sources
- [ ] ≥2 Tier-1 sources (official docs, RFCs, framework org)
- [ ] ≥2 Tier-2 sources (GitHub ≥500 stars, maintained ≤12 months)
- [ ] Source URLs are real and relevant (not generic)
- [ ] No Tier-4 sources (tutorial sites, beginner content)

### Code Examples
- [ ] ≥5 code pattern pairs (✅ DO + ❌ DON'T)
- [ ] Code is specific to {{ .StackName }} / {{ .FrameworkVersion }} (not pseudocode)
- [ ] Language-tagged code blocks
- [ ] Examples are illustrative of the actual pattern, not trivial

### Anti-Patterns
- [ ] ≥3 named anti-patterns with explanations
- [ ] Anti-patterns are realistic (things real developers actually do wrong)

### Completeness
- [ ] All required sections present (Sources, Core Rules, Code Patterns, Anti-Patterns, Key Decisions, Checklist)
- [ ] ≥8 core rules
- [ ] ≥10 checklist items
- [ ] Content is specific to this stack's version (not generic "use TypeScript" advice)

### Accuracy
- [ ] No invented code examples (everything traceable to sources)
- [ ] Advice is current for {{ .FrameworkVersion }} (not deprecated APIs)
- [ ] No contradictions between topics in this cycle

